# Card copy (all roles)

Follow this for **every** visible line: lifeSg `title` / `subheader` / `how`, catalogue `whatFor`, permit pack rows, quiz card points.

`title` is the **topic** of the card: **3–5 words**. Name the subject. Do not restate the bullets (no verb + same job). Same title for every role when it is the same piece of content. No catalogue-speak (“Shared”, “Gathered”, “Confirmation of”).

`lead` is a **2–4 word** action line under the title. Verb first. Same job as the bullets, compressed. Do **not** replace the bullets. Write three versions — tenant, contractor, Project Officer.

Bullets stay the task lines. Write **three** versions of each card’s bullets — tenant, contractor, Project Officer. Same job. That reader’s moves only.

Keys in `process-v10-copy.ts` must match catalogue `stage.name::step.name` exactly. A missed key falls back to a long paragraph — that is a fail.

## Prompt

Rewrite each line for a busy reader who is not fluent in English. The reader is the **current login**: tenant, contractor, or Project Officer.

**Pass only if all are true:**

1. First word is **their** verb: Go, Be, Bring, Fill, Apply, Create, Book, Ask, Send, Email, Submit, Install, Upload, Fix, Measure, Confirm, Use, Read, Do, Get, Leave, Note, Select, Approve, Register, Present, Walk, Collect, Sign, Lodge, Complete, Hand, Settle, Attend, Revise, Remind, Advise, Compile, Share, Check, Schedule, Tell, Start, Link, Monitor, Issue, Review, Notify, Update, Request.
2. **4–10 words.** Count. Prefer 7–8. Cut extras.
3. **They do this.** Not someone else. Fold a handoff into Get (it arrives to them) or Check (they can look in a named system). Never “Wait for…” — it sounds like nothing to do. Never “X sends…”, “X will…”, “sits with…”, “You’ll get…”, “You do not…”.
4. Same sitting, same verb, same system = **one point**. Example: apply for terminal access and unit access → “Apply for terminal and unit access in OneCalendar.” Split only when the actor, system, or wait changes.
5. Simple words. No “so that”, “in order to”, “if you can”, “kindly”.
6. You / your. Calm supervisor. No slang. No legal.
7. Keep names they must open: OneCalendar, IFM, AES, Project Officer, TOPAZ, URA. Officer may name CAG-internal tools they use (OneDrive, Newforma, SharePoint, Key Management System, Procurement). Never show those tools to tenant or contractor.
8. That meeting’s title is **KickOff meeting** (the term they use). Never bare “kickoff”. Stage chrome may still say Kickoff.
9. Do not invent steps or slugs. Same job, fewer words.
10. One bullet = one move for **this** reader. Lists of drawings, report types, or pack contents are not tasks — fold them.

Fail and rewrite: starts with a name or “You will”; explains someone else; two different jobs; over 10 words; “You do not…”.

## Role

- **Tenant** — their apply / approve / send / attend / lodge. If they only receive, one Get line with who or where (`hideOnlyIf` if they have no move). Check if they can look in a system.
- **Contractor** — site and OneCalendar moves. Never tenancy/ops cards already `hideFrom: ["contractor"]`.
- **Project Officer** — their compile / advise / schedule / approve / send. Internal retrieve is allowed. If IFM or AES does the work, one Check/Get line — do not narrate their job.

## Good

- Title: OneCalendar for the unit. Bullet: Approve unit access in OneCalendar when asked.
- Title: Design pack approval. Same title for tenant, contractor, and Project Officer.
- Approve unit access in OneCalendar when asked.
- Apply for terminal and unit access in OneCalendar.
- Create tenant, brand, and outlet records in OneCalendar.
- Go to the first site meeting when invited.
- Send one design pack to your Project Officer.
- Get written design approval before permits.
- Submit all remaining permits together in OneCalendar.
- Walk the unit with IFM at handover.

## Bad

- Your contractor applies in OneCalendar. You’ll approve their unit access.
- Apply for terminal access in OneCalendar. / Apply for unit access in OneCalendar.
- Project Officer sends the time and place.
- You’ll get the kickoff pack before site requirements are confirmed.
- Coloured perspectives / Architectural plans / Ceiling layout (inventory, not tasks)
- Building Maintenance will endorse the form.
- You do not submit these yourself.
